# menu.zd — a navigation menu, and the menu that is not here.
#
# ⚠️ THERE IS NO ACTION MENU IN THIS FILE, AND THERE CANNOT BE.
#
# What a program usually means by "menu" is a button that opens a list of
# *commands*, closes when one is picked, closes on Escape, closes when the
# pointer goes elsewhere, and moves focus into the list so the arrow keys
# work. Every one of those five needs something the language does not have:
#
#   * `aria-expanded` and `aria-haspopup` on the trigger — unspellable,
#     because an argument name admits no hyphen (§16.3.6).
#   * close on select — the trigger would have to be a `Truth` signal and
#     an `if`, which is expressible, but see the point above: a
#     hand-rolled disclosure with no `aria-expanded` announces nothing.
#   * close on Escape — a keystroke is only delivered to the focused
#     element, and after a pointer click on the trigger the focus is the
#     trigger. Nothing can move it.
#   * close on click-outside — there is no document-level listener; `on`
#     attaches to the element it is written under.
#   * arrow keys within the list — needs a roving `tabindex` and a way to
#     call `focus`. Neither exists.
#
# So the action menu is written up in the README as not expressible rather
# than shipped broken. What *is* here is the other menu, and it is a real
# and complete pattern rather than a consolation: the W3C disclosure
# navigation menu, which is a `details` holding a list of links.
#
# It is complete because the browser owns all of it. A `summary` is exposed
# as a button with `aria-expanded` maintained by the user agent — the one
# route by which this language gets that attribute at all — it is operable
# by keyboard with no handler, and the pattern does not ask for arrow keys,
# because Tab through a short list of links is the specified behaviour.
# Closing on select is moot: following a link ends this program instance
# and begins another at the target document (§14G.2).

record MenuLink
    label is Text
    href  is Text

component NavMenu with label, links, class, linkClass
    Details class is class
        Summary label
        List
            each link in links
                Item
                    Link link.href, class is linkClass
                        Text link.label
